      "writtenOn": "2017-01-30T17:54:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is kind of confusing.\nThis |ScannerImpl| class is valid only if associated client interface class is alive.\nThe Invalid() call happens here:\nhttp://cs/android/system/connectivity/wificond/client_interface_impl.cpp?l\u003d108\u0026rcl\u003d7b6642b45c51d4cac41fb7626a4080ce181415aa\n\nWe know that in a destructor, the body executes firstly, and then it destroys member variables.\nIn this case, |Invalid()| comes first, and then |scanner_| destructor of is called, and then |unsubscribePnoScanEvent()| is called. Here we should allow the cleanup of subscriptions to happen even if the associated client interface class was dead.\n\nBottom line:\nIt makes sens and is useful for a cleanup function to be run even if we find things are incoherent.",
      "revId": "3e784e279c2a2afc48db4b14c9a73e60f9e50766",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
